    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.44,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.1,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.42 from 6 h onward, which could mean either stationary phase or reader saturation. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test this. A 10x dilution read 0.0432 (0.0472 and 0.0392), which scales to 0.43. A 3x dilution read 0.154 (0.160 and 0.148), which scales to 0.46. Both scaled values are close to the undiluted 0.42, within the roughly ±0.005 read noise multiplied by the dilution factor. If the reader were saturating, the diluted samples would scale to well above 0.42, for example 0.6 or more. They do not, so the plateau looks like genuine stationary phase and the undiluted readings are about right."
  },
